{"id": "111", "question": "What is the last letter written in the image?", "gt": "The last letter is \"a\".", "pred": "E", "group_key": "visual challenge", "sub_category": "visual challenge", "dataset": "haloquest", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "E", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUpon examination of the image, the letter 'E' is formed by a series of red, cylindrical shapes arranged vertically. These shapes are positioned at the bottom right corner of the image. The structure and alignment of these shapes constitute the final letter visible in the image.\nThe letter 'E' is composed of three horizontal bars and one vertical bar on the left.\n The top horizontal bar is at the top of the letter.\n The middle horizontal bar is in the middle of the letter.\n The bottom horizontal bar is at the bottom of the letter.\n The vertical bar is on the left side, connecting the three horizontal bars.\n These components are made of red cylinders arranged in a specific pattern.\n This arrangement is located in the bottom right corner of the image.\n No other letters are present after this arrangement.\nThe arrangement of the red cylinders at the bottom right corner of the image conforms to the standard letterform 'E'. It is constructed with three horizontal bars and one vertical bar on the left side. The top, middle, and bottom horizontal bars are aligned with the vertical bar, forming a complete letter. This structure is the final element in the composition of the image.\n\nE", "time_sec": 340.142, "generation_time_seconds": 266.3021, "selection_time_seconds": 72.4606, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
